                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "91b084cf-85f4-427e-94a0-222913da6cff",
                        "source_entry_id": "de247a1f-d477-39c5-a8b5-28e06e7da4e6",
                        "source_sense_id": "0fc6f1e3-66e2-360a-9a04-990ec5bbf5e5",
                        "source_sense_description": "Staatsbürgerin von Dänemark: Dänin",
                        "target_lang_word": "Dänin",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Dänin",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "75b3ef7c-305a-3d5c-a4e4-1ed915aa0830",
                                        "entry_id": "24a3ab23-d3ec-3745-b1cd-72eb4ad5ee13",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Staatsbürgerin von Dänemark"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ccf5c3fe-48f8-4742-8e2a-57f49c7be421",
                                                "sense_id": "75b3ef7c-305a-3d5c-a4e4-1ed915aa0830",
                                                "text": "„Du machst dich an eine Dänin ran.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "34205773-af23-4e35-a209-6cf7957641cd",
                                                "sense_id": "75b3ef7c-305a-3d5c-a4e4-1ed915aa0830",
                                                "text": "„Katrine ist Anfang dreißig, eine schlanke blonde Dänin mit spöttischen grünen Augen, einem Bubikopf und einem ausgesprochenen Hang zur Arktis.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e19a743d-be61-40fe-8420-7bd7ceba7731",
                                                "sense_id": "75b3ef7c-305a-3d5c-a4e4-1ed915aa0830",
                                                "text": "„Sie ist Dänin und heißt Tove, wie die Schriftstellerin, und sie lässt euch grüßen.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "492d510e-939c-43a5-a88d-3babe3e267e9",
                        "source_entry_id": "de247a1f-d477-39c5-a8b5-28e06e7da4e6",
                        "source_sense_id": "0fc6f1e3-66e2-360a-9a04-990ec5bbf5e5",
                        "source_sense_description": "Staatsbürgerin von Dänemark: Dänin",
                        "target_lang_word": "Dane",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Dane",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e50b2331-77cc-3ad8-92e8-b0c08cb829e0",
                                        "entry_id": "c86ef925-186f-3a19-adad-f68e5332e9a7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A surname transferred from the nickname for someone who came from Denmark, also a variant of Dean."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7a898bb2-20a3-41d0-89e8-8f15303e83f5",
                                                "sense_id": "e50b2331-77cc-3ad8-92e8-b0c08cb829e0",
                                                "text": "Often he wrote good ones on casual slips and fancied them his; names like Trevellyan or Montressor or Delancey, with musical prefixes; or a good, short, beautiful, but dignified name like \"Gordon Dane\". He liked that one. It suggested something."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f54fb67-533a-4985-b99c-78dd6b36a77e",
                                                "sense_id": "e50b2331-77cc-3ad8-92e8-b0c08cb829e0",
                                                "text": "In “Euphoria,” Dane plays Cal Jacobs, the troubled father to Jacob Elordi’s character in the HBO drama, which is scheduled to begin production on its third season on April 14."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b796c6a6-b37a-3e44-a997-23b940579052",
                                        "entry_id": "c86ef925-186f-3a19-adad-f68e5332e9a7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A male given name transferred from the surname, or from the ethnic term Dane (like Scott or Norman)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "002b4f0e-8900-4d81-8c9c-3b14d642cdea",
                                                "sense_id": "b796c6a6-b37a-3e44-a997-23b940579052",
                                                "text": "\"I'm going to call him Dane.\"\n\"What a queer name! Why? Is it an O'Neill family name? I thought you were finished with the O'Neills.\"\n\"It's got nothing to do with Luke. This is his name, no one else's. - - - I called Justine Justine simply because I liked the name, and I'm calling Dane Dane for the same reason.\"\n\"Well, it does have a nice ring to it,\" Fee admitted."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f6c3a61d-4b8b-332e-80db-428c311d04e7",
                                        "entry_id": "c86ef925-186f-3a19-adad-f68e5332e9a7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A river, the River Dane, in Cheshire, England, which joins the River Weaver at Northwich."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Dane",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3a5e2d64-1009-313d-8933-5df6cbaccef9",
                                        "entry_id": "8e7b8a0a-7a75-30f2-aa28-478e611930ce",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person of Danish descent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "71db0bee-4545-4106-9f3e-3b8b9f7222a3",
                                                "sense_id": "3a5e2d64-1009-313d-8933-5df6cbaccef9",
                                                "text": "Fresleven - that was the fellow’s name, a Dane - thought himself wronged somehow in the bargain, so he went ashore and started to hammer the chief of the village with a stick."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bb00125a-7e31-3792-9226-b83fa5d9ad30",
                                        "entry_id": "8e7b8a0a-7a75-30f2-aa28-478e611930ce",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person from Denmark."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74869ca2-5a81-4d18-9fc6-8437fcfb2907",
                                                "sense_id": "bb00125a-7e31-3792-9226-b83fa5d9ad30",
                                                "text": "As Denmark takes over the presidency of the European Union, Danes are more strongly pro-European than at any time in the past two decades – a shift in sentiment that can at least partly be attributed to US President Donald Trump."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "58b63ccc-d330-3285-949e-a1df4462f6ab",
                                        "entry_id": "8e7b8a0a-7a75-30f2-aa28-478e611930ce",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In Anglo-Saxon England, any of the seafaring raiders and settlers who attacked and colonized parts of England from the late 8th century onward; a Viking."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "576be880-f9b2-34ef-8c60-d006e0576f54",
                                        "entry_id": "8e7b8a0a-7a75-30f2-aa28-478e611930ce",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A member of the Danes, a Germanic tribe inhabiting the Danish islands and parts of southern Sweden."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "58c2bf3e-2df9-4597-ab5b-0f11a17c1f2d",
                                                "sense_id": "576be880-f9b2-34ef-8c60-d006e0576f54",
                                                "text": "Kenett states that the military works still known by the name of Tadmarten Camp and Hook-Norton Barrow were cast up at this time; the former, large and round, is judged to be a fortification of the Danes, and the latter, being smaller and rather a quinquangle than a square, of the Saxons."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "da60e266-eafc-4a89-a5d9-c34ce23b962c",
                                                "sense_id": "576be880-f9b2-34ef-8c60-d006e0576f54",
                                                "text": "I have wrestled the hilt\nfrom the enemies' hand, avenged the evil\ndone to the Danes; it is what is due."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bd469c8b-8bb6-42c7-9b22-15e7eccbbada",
                        "source_entry_id": "de247a1f-d477-39c5-a8b5-28e06e7da4e6",
                        "source_sense_id": "0fc6f1e3-66e2-360a-9a04-990ec5bbf5e5",
                        "source_sense_description": "Staatsbürgerin von Dänemark: Dänin",
                        "target_lang_word": "датчанка",
                        "target_lang_code": "ru",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "датчанка",
                                "target_lang_code": "ru",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "17a08d4c-de37-3dbf-bed5-b9eb8bb20da6",
                                        "entry_id": "23934bcd-4994-3074-9721-dfb45b974c4e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "женск. к датчанин: жительница, уроженка или женщина-потомок уроженцев Дании"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a39056fc-eb1c-415b-9b12-56935f26974a",
                                                "sense_id": "17a08d4c-de37-3dbf-bed5-b9eb8bb20da6",
                                                "text": "Один из ближних столиков заняла чопорная благообразная старушка в седых буклях, в дорогих черных шелках, и при ней барышня лет шестнадцати: красивое, здоровое созданье, кровь с молоком, датчанка или норвежка, с коровьими глазами и бюстом, как бастион."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "38115ff2-8f2f-4282-b0fb-532e3efa2ded",
                                                "sense_id": "17a08d4c-de37-3dbf-bed5-b9eb8bb20da6",
                                                "text": "Ему не хотелось говорить дурно даже о том, кто сейчас воевал против России и был всегда врагом маленькой Дании, а следовательно, и царицы-матери как датчанки."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8fc7b280-7feb-4621-ab93-f2b32d16281d",
                                                "sense_id": "17a08d4c-de37-3dbf-bed5-b9eb8bb20da6",
                                                "text": "Я понял то наслаждение, с которым вдовствующая императрица Мария Федоровна, родом датчанка, освобождала себя ежегодно на несколько недель от «русского плена», чтобы иметь возможность побегать на свободе по магазинам своего родного Копенгагена."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "46dc726a-e9d5-4669-a934-735151482dbf",
                                                "sense_id": "17a08d4c-de37-3dbf-bed5-b9eb8bb20da6",
                                                "text": "Многие француженки и турчанки покупают обувь 39-го размера, шведки и англичанки ― 40-го, датчанки ― 41-го размера."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
